From 94ef85811504c062be78a162bb62f520e18253c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 04:19:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] reldist, subtract, flank: keep 64-bit coordinates (large
 chromosomes)

Since 2.28 coordinates are 64-bit (CHRPOS), but three tools still narrowed
them to 32-bit int, so on chromosomes with coordinates above 2^31 (~2.15 Gb;
common in plant, amphibian and some fish genomes):

  reldist  LoadMidpoints/CalculateRelativeDistance cast (bed.end + bed.start)
           to int before halving, so every query whose start+end >= 2^31 was
           silently dropped from the distribution.
  subtract subtractHits held keyStart/keyEnd/hitStart/hitEnd and the block
           coordinates in int, producing negative end coordinates.
  flank    AddFlank/AddStrandedFlank took chromSize and the flank sizes as int
           and compared with static_cast<int>, collapsing the flanks to
           [0, feature.start).

Use CHRPOS throughout these three code paths.

test/{reldist,subtract,flank}/: a large-chromosome case each (coordinates
around 3e9), failing on unmodified master and passing with this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TaHntBDKuZJpMAAMenkC44
